; pi4HdmiAudioTone.pi4 - the smallest thing that could prove sound.
;
; DIAGNOSTIC. Does not ship. THIS ONE WRITES REGISTERS AND MAKES A NOISE.
;
; A fixed tone, a known number of samples, played once. Not a wav
; player, not a mixer, no streaming and no double buffering. The whole
; program is one measurement and five short bursts of square wave, and
; the verdict is a person saying whether they heard anything.
;
; Run pi4HdmiAudioProbe.pi4 FIRST. It reads and writes nothing, and if
; it says the link is not ready this program cannot work and will say so
; and stop.
;
;   PureMetalForge.exe --compile RaspberryPi4/Examples/Diagnostics/NotBuilding/pi4HdmiAudioTone.pi4 -t pi4 \
;        --load-addr 0x400000 --stack-addr 0x3000000 --entry-returns \
;        -o tone.img
;
; ----------------------------------------------------------------------
;  BE HONEST ABOUT WHAT THIS PROVES. IT IS NOT THE USUAL EVIDENCE.
; ----------------------------------------------------------------------
;  Every other bring-up in this project was settled by reading bytes
;  back on the CPU. A SPEAKER CANNOT BE READ BACK. So this program is
;  explicit about which of its claims are machine-checked and which are
;  not, and it prints them in that order:
;
;    MACHINE-CHECKED, and it happens first:
;      * the registers were configured and read back
;      * THE FIFO DRAINS AT THE RATE IT SHOULD - see below. This is the
;        real result of this program and it needs no ears.
;      * the underflow and overflow latches in MAI_CTL, after the fact
;      * FRAME_COUNT advanced while audio was playing, so the blanking
;        intervals the samples ride in were really going by
;
;    NOT MACHINE-CHECKED, and nothing here can make it so:
;      * that anything came out of the speaker. IT WAS REPORTED
;        HEARING A TONE, OR DOES NOT. That is the final step and it is a
;        human one.
;
;  A STATUS BIT MUST NOT BE ALLOWED TO STAND IN FOR THE LAST ONE. At the
;  V3D stage on this same board every register reported success while
;  the output page was still poison. "MAI_CTL says ENABLE and there was
;  no underrun" is not a sound.
;
; ----------------------------------------------------------------------
;  WHY THE DRAIN MEASUREMENT COMES BEFORE THE TONE
; ----------------------------------------------------------------------
;  The 108 MHz MAI clock is not a firmware clock and cannot be asked
;  about down the mailbox - see the long note in pi4HdmiAudioProbe.pi4.
;  The only thing readable there is a gate bit, and on this platform a
;  gate or power bit means "some client has claimed this", not "the
;  hardware is running": GET_CLOCK_STATE once said off for a clock
;  GET_CLOCK_MEASURED reported at 250000496 Hz.
;
;  The measurement that does exist is downstream. Feed the FIFO as fast
;  as it will take words and time a known count against CNTPCT_EL0:
;
;    predicted rate = 108000000 / MAI_SMP_N * channels
;                   = 108000000 / 2250 * 2   = 96000 words per second
;
;  One word is one IEC 60958 subframe is one channel's sample
;  (vc4_hdmi.c:2168 - the DAI accepts only
;  SNDRV_PCM_FMTBIT_IEC958_SUBFRAME_LE), so stereo takes two words per
;  frame. THAT ONE NUMBER SETTLES FOUR THINGS AT ONCE: the 108 MHz clock
;  is really oscillating, MAI_SMP holds the divider we think it does,
;  the CPU may feed MAI_DATA at all, and a word is a subframe rather
;  than a packed stereo pair. None of the four needed a status bit to be
;  believed, and none of the four needed a speaker.
;
;  HOW TO READ THE NUMBER:
;    near 96000  everything above holds. This is the good answer.
;    near 48000  the first three hold; the fourth does not, and one word
;                is a whole stereo frame. Segment 4 below is the one to
;                listen to.
;    steady but far from either - the MAI is running at a rate nobody
;                programmed. Suspect MAI_SMP first, the 108 MHz fixed
;                clock second, and do not touch the audio data.
;    zero, or the first write fails with EFIFOFULL - nothing is draining
;                the FIFO. Either the MAI is not running or the CPU may
;                not write MAI_DATA. STOP: no change to the waveform can
;                fix this and every minute spent on samples is wasted.
;
; ----------------------------------------------------------------------
;  WHY THERE ARE FIVE SEGMENTS AND NOT ONE TONE
; ----------------------------------------------------------------------
;  What a MAI_DATA word must CONTAIN is settled - an IEC 60958 subframe.
;  The BIT NUMBERING inside that subframe is not, because the standard
;  is not on this machine and is not free to fetch, and neither is what
;  MAI_CONFIG's BIT_REVERSE and FORMAT_REVERSE (vc4_regs.h:522-523) do
;  to the bits on the way out. HdmiAudioStart() sets both because
;  vc4_hdmi_audio_prepare() sets both, and no source here says what
;  either one reverses.
;
;  Guessing once and hearing silence teaches nothing - it cannot tell a
;  wrong layout from a dead path. So the same tone is played five times,
;  each through a different candidate encoding, announced over the UART
;  before it starts and separated by a gap of digital silence. THE
;  VERDICT IS WHICH SEGMENT MADE A NOISE, which is something a person
;  can report without instruments. Silence in all five, with the drain
;  measuring 96000, is also a result: it means the samples are leaving
;  the FIFO and not reaching the wire, and the next place to look is the
;  audio packet slot and AUDIO_PACKET_CONFIG's channel mask, not the
;  samples.
;
;  A rejected alternative was to play one segment per run and rebuild
;  between them. Five runs, five power cycles, five chances to change
;  something else by accident, and whoever is listening holds four previous
;  results in their head. One run with announced segments is the same
;  experiment with the confounds removed.
;
;  NOISE RATHER THAN A CLEAN TONE IS STILL A PASS. It means samples
;  reached the sink and only the layout is wrong, which is enormously
;  more progress than silence.
;
; ----------------------------------------------------------------------
;  WHAT THE TONE IS
; ----------------------------------------------------------------------
;  1 kHz square wave, one eighth of full scale, 48 kHz stereo, the same
;  sample in both channels.
;
;  SQUARE AND NOT SINE, deliberately. A sine needs a table, and a table
;  is one more thing that can be wrong in a program whose entire job is
;  to distinguish "wrong" from "dead". A square wave is two constants
;  and a counter, it is the loudest thing per unit amplitude, and it
;  survives severe mangling and is still audible - which is exactly the
;  property wanted when the encoding is under test.
;
;  1 kHz and not 440 Hz: 48000 divides by 1000 exactly, so the half
;  period is 24 samples with no remainder and no accumulating phase
;  error over the whole burst. 440 Hz would have needed a fractional
;  divider, and a drifting one would have been indistinguishable from a
;  clock problem.
;
;  ONE EIGHTH OF FULL SCALE and not full scale: a full-scale square wave
;  through an unknown encoding into a monitor's speakers at whatever
;  volume it happens to be set to is how equipment and ears get hurt. A
;  quiet tone that is audible is enough to answer the question.

XIncludeFile "RaspberryPi4/Lib/hdmiaudio.pi4"

#UART_DR = $FE201000
#UART_FR = $FE201018

; The tone. All four numbers are here so that changing one does not
; require reading the loop.
#TONE_RATE      = 48000
#TONE_CHANNELS  = 2
#TONE_HALFCYCLE = 24            ; 48000 / 1000 / 2 - a 1 kHz square
#TONE_AMPLITUDE = $100000       ; 1/8 of a 24-bit full scale ($800000)

; Half a second of stereo at 48 kHz, in WORDS. One word per channel per
; sample, so 48000 * 2 / 2.
#TONE_WORDS  = 48000
; A quarter second of digital silence between segments, same units.
#GAP_WORDS   = 24000
; The drain measurement's sample size. Half a second at the predicted
; rate - long enough that the initial FIFO fill is a rounding error,
; short enough that nobody is waiting.
#DRAIN_WORDS = 48000

#SEGMENTS = 5

Procedure PutC(c.i)
  Define f.i
  Repeat
    f = PeekN(#UART_FR)
  Until (f & 32) = 0
  PokeL(#UART_DR, c)
EndProcedure

Procedure PutS(*s)
  Define i.i
  Define c.i
  i = 0
  Repeat
    ; PeekA, not PeekB. PeekB names the SIGNED .b and sign-extends, so
    ; a byte above 127 would come back negative and this loop would
    ; never see its terminator.
    c = PeekA(*s + i)
    If c = 0 : Break : EndIf
    PutC(c)
    i = i + 1
  ForEver
EndProcedure

Procedure PutNl()
  PutC(13) : PutC(10)
EndProcedure

Procedure PutHex(v.i, digits.i)
  Define i.i
  Define n.i
  For i = digits - 1 To 0 Step -1
    n = (v >> (i * 4)) & $F
    If n < 10
      PutC(48 + n)
    Else
      PutC(55 + n)
    EndIf
  Next
EndProcedure

Procedure PutDec(v.i)
  Define d.i
  Define started.i
  Define digit.i
  If v < 0
    PutC(45)
    v = 0 - v
  EndIf
  If v = 0
    PutC(48)
    ProcedureReturn
  EndIf
  d = 1000000000000000000
  started = 0
  While d > 0
    digit = (v / d) % 10
    If digit <> 0 Or started = 1
      PutC(48 + digit)
      started = 1
    EndIf
    d = d / 10
  Wend
EndProcedure

; ----------------------------------------------------------------------
;  The architectural counter, read here rather than borrowed.
;
;  Under a private Tone* prefix and NOT taken from timer.pi4, because
;  house rule 10 says the main file lists the libraries it uses and this
;  one uses exactly one. Pulling in timer.pi4 for two instructions would
;  add a whole library to the build to save four lines.
; ----------------------------------------------------------------------
Procedure.i ToneTicks()
  ASM
    mrs x0, cntpct_el0
  EndASM
EndProcedure

Procedure.i ToneHz()
  ASM
    mrs x0, cntfrq_el0
  EndASM
EndProcedure

; ----------------------------------------------------------------------
;  THE FIVE CANDIDATE ENCODINGS.
;
;  Each takes a 24-bit signed sample and returns the 32-bit word to
;  store. They are ordered most-likely-first, so a listener who hears
;  segment 1 can stop paying attention.
; ----------------------------------------------------------------------

; 1. The canonical IEC 60958 subframe, built by the library: sample at
;    bits 4..27, V/U/C clear, even parity at bit 31. This is what
;    vc4_hdmi.c:2168 says the hardware is fed.
Procedure.i EncSubframe(s.i)
  ProcedureReturn HdmiAudioSubframe(s, 0)
EndProcedure

; 2. The same subframe with all 32 bits reversed. The obvious reading of
;    MAI_CONFIG's BIT_REVERSE is that the hardware reverses the bits on
;    the way out, in which case handing it a pre-reversed word cancels
;    the transform and the wire sees a correct subframe.
;
;    Done with a shift loop and not the RBIT instruction. RBIT would be
;    one cycle, but this runs 96000 times a second on a 600 MHz part at
;    worst - thirty-two shifts is under a microsecond and the deadline
;    is ten - and a plain loop cannot be got wrong the way a hand-written
;    inline instruction with the wrong register can.
Procedure.i EncBitReversed(s.i)
  Define v.i
  Define r.i
  Define i.i
  v = HdmiAudioSubframe(s, 0)
  r = 0
  i = 0
  While i < 32
    r = (r << 1) | ((v >> i) & 1)
    i = i + 1
  Wend
  ProcedureReturn r & $FFFFFFFF
EndProcedure

; 3. The subframe with its bytes swapped. If FORMAT_REVERSE turns out to
;    be an endianness swap rather than a bit one, this is the word that
;    arrives correct.
Procedure.i EncByteSwapped(s.i)
  Define v.i
  v = HdmiAudioSubframe(s, 0)
  ProcedureReturn (((v & $FF) << 24) | ((v & $FF00) << 8) | ((v >> 8) & $FF00) | ((v >> 24) & $FF)) & $FFFFFFFF
EndProcedure

; 4. NO IEC FRAMING AT ALL: a packed 16-bit stereo pair, the same sample
;    in both halves. This is the hypothesis the drain measurement tests
;    directly - if one word is a whole frame rather than one subframe,
;    the measured rate is 48000 rather than 96000 and this is the
;    encoding to listen for. It is included even when the rate says
;    96000 because a rate is about how many words are consumed and this
;    is about what is in them, and those can be wrong independently.
Procedure.i EncPacked16(s.i)
  Define h.i
  h = (s >> 8) & $FFFF
  ProcedureReturn ((h << 16) | h) & $FFFFFFFF
EndProcedure

; 5. A bare 24-bit sample left-justified in the word, no framing bits at
;    all. The last resort: it is what the register would want if the
;    IEC reading is wrong in some way none of the above covers, and it
;    is cheap to include.
Procedure.i EncRaw24(s.i)
  ProcedureReturn ((s & $FFFFFF) << 8) & $FFFFFFFF
EndProcedure

Procedure.i Encode(which.i, s.i)
  If which = 1 : ProcedureReturn EncSubframe(s) : EndIf
  If which = 2 : ProcedureReturn EncBitReversed(s) : EndIf
  If which = 3 : ProcedureReturn EncByteSwapped(s) : EndIf
  If which = 4 : ProcedureReturn EncPacked16(s) : EndIf
  ProcedureReturn EncRaw24(s)
EndProcedure

; Written as a plain chain of Ifs rather than as early returns: a bare
; ProcedureReturn with no value cannot be followed by a statement
; separator on the same line, and spreading five early returns over
; twenty lines to work around that is worse than five tests.
Procedure PutEncName(which.i)
  If which = 1
    PutS("IEC 60958 subframe, as the driver's format says")
  EndIf
  If which = 2
    PutS("the same subframe, all 32 bits reversed")
  EndIf
  If which = 3
    PutS("the same subframe, bytes swapped")
  EndIf
  If which = 4
    PutS("no framing - a packed 16-bit stereo pair")
  EndIf
  If which = 5
    PutS("no framing - a bare 24-bit sample, left justified")
  EndIf
EndProcedure

; ----------------------------------------------------------------------
;  THE MEASUREMENT. Push words of digital silence and time them.
;
;  Silence and not tone, because this runs before anybody is asked to
;  listen and a half second of square wave nobody was warned about is
;  rude. It measures the same thing either way - the FIFO does not care
;  what is in the words.
;
;  Returns words per second, or 0 if it could not be measured.
; ----------------------------------------------------------------------
Procedure.i MeasureDrain(words.i)
  Define t0.i
  Define t1.i
  Define hz.i
  Define i.i
  Define quiet.i

  hz = ToneHz()
  If hz = 0
    PutS("  CNTFRQ_EL0 reads zero - there is no clock to measure against.")
    PutNl()
    ProcedureReturn 0
  EndIf

  quiet = HdmiAudioSubframe(0, 0)

  ; PRIME THE FIFO FIRST, AND DO NOT COUNT IT. The first few dozen
  ; writes go into an empty FIFO at memory speed and would make the
  ; measured rate look enormous if they were inside the timed window.
  ; Writing until FULL puts the loop in the steady state the timing is
  ; supposed to describe.
  i = 0
  While HdmiAudioSpace() <> 0
    If HdmiAudioWriteWord(quiet) = 0
      PutS("  the priming write failed: ") : PutS(HdmiAudioErrorText()) : PutNl()
      ProcedureReturn 0
    EndIf
    i = i + 1
    ; A FIFO that never fills is a FIFO that is draining infinitely
    ; fast, which means it is not a FIFO. Bound it rather than hang.
    If i > 4096
      PutS("  the FIFO never reported FULL after 4096 words.") : PutNl()
      PutS("  Either FULL is not where we think it is, or nothing is") : PutNl()
      PutS("  being buffered at all.") : PutNl()
      Break
    EndIf
  Wend

  t0 = ToneTicks()
  i = 0
  While i < words
    If HdmiAudioWriteWord(quiet) = 0
      PutS("  write ") : PutDec(i) : PutS(" failed: ")
      PutS(HdmiAudioErrorText()) : PutNl()
      ProcedureReturn 0
    EndIf
    i = i + 1
  Wend
  t1 = ToneTicks()

  If t1 = t0
    PutS("  the whole burst took zero ticks - nothing is throttling us,") : PutNl()
    PutS("  which means the FIFO is not draining, it is discarding.") : PutNl()
    ProcedureReturn 0
  EndIf

  ; words * hz / elapsed, with the multiply first so the division does
  ; not round the answer to nothing. words is 48000 and hz is 54000000,
  ; so the product is about 2.6e12 - comfortable in 64 bits.
  ProcedureReturn (words * hz) / (t1 - t0)
EndProcedure

; ----------------------------------------------------------------------
;  One segment: a known number of words of 1 kHz square wave through one
;  candidate encoding, then a gap of silence.
;
;  Returns 1 if every write was accepted.
; ----------------------------------------------------------------------
Procedure.i PlaySegment(which.i)
  Define i.i
  Define phase.i
  Define sample.i
  Define w.i
  Define ch.i
  Define quiet.i

  phase = 0
  sample = #TONE_AMPLITUDE
  i = 0
  While i < #TONE_WORDS
    ; One sample, then the same sample again for the second channel.
    ; CHANNEL ORDER IS NOT KNOWN AND DOES NOT MATTER HERE: both
    ; channels carry identical data precisely so that a swapped pair
    ; cannot be mistaken for a failure.
    w = Encode(which, sample)
    ch = 0
    While ch < #TONE_CHANNELS
      If HdmiAudioWriteWord(w) = 0
        PutNl()
        PutS("  write failed at word ") : PutDec(i) : PutS(": ")
        PutS(HdmiAudioErrorText()) : PutNl()
        ProcedureReturn 0
      EndIf
      ch = ch + 1
    Wend
    i = i + #TONE_CHANNELS

    phase = phase + 1
    If phase >= #TONE_HALFCYCLE
      phase = 0
      sample = 0 - sample
    EndIf
  Wend

  ; The gap. Digital silence, not a stopped stream: stopping and
  ; restarting the MAI between segments would re-run all of
  ; HdmiAudioStart()'s register writes and make each segment a
  ; different experiment.
  quiet = HdmiAudioSubframe(0, 0)
  i = 0
  While i < #GAP_WORDS
    If HdmiAudioWriteWord(quiet) = 0
      ProcedureReturn 0
    EndIf
    i = i + 1
  Wend

  ProcedureReturn 1
EndProcedure

Procedure.i Main()
  Define st.i
  Define rate.i
  Define which.i
  Define f0.i
  Define f1.i
  Define ok.i

  PutNl()
  PutS("=== pi4HdmiAudioTone - THIS ONE MAKES A NOISE ===") : PutNl()
  PutNl()

  st = HdmiAudioSelfTest()
  If st <> 0
    PutS("HdmiAudioSelfTest() FAILED at check ") : PutDec(st) : PutNl()
    ProcedureReturn 100 + st
  EndIf

  ; Port 0 first, then port 1 if nothing is plugged into 0. Which
  ; socket is which is not established anywhere - see
  ; pi4HdmiAudioProbe.pi4 - so this program finds out rather than
  ; assuming.
  If HdmiAudioInit(0) = 0
    PutS("init(0) failed: ") : PutS(HdmiAudioErrorText()) : PutNl()
    ProcedureReturn 1
  EndIf
  HdmiAudioProbe()
  If HdmiAudioHotplug() = 0
    PutS("port 0 reports nothing plugged in - trying port 1.") : PutNl()
    If HdmiAudioInit(1) = 0
      PutS("init(1) failed: ") : PutS(HdmiAudioErrorText()) : PutNl()
      ProcedureReturn 2
    EndIf
    HdmiAudioProbe()
  EndIf
  PutS("using port ") : PutDec(HdmiAudioPort()) : PutNl()

  If HdmiAudioLinkReady() = 0
    PutS("THE LINK IS NOT READY: ") : PutS(HdmiAudioErrorText()) : PutNl()
    PutS("Audio rides in the blanking intervals of a running picture.") : PutNl()
    PutS("Run pi4HdmiAudioProbe.pi4 and read the four preconditions.") : PutNl()
    ProcedureReturn 3
  EndIf

  ; ------------------------------------------------------------------
  ;  Configure. This is the first write of the program.
  ; ------------------------------------------------------------------
  If HdmiAudioStart(#TONE_RATE, #TONE_CHANNELS) = 0
    PutS("HdmiAudioStart failed: ") : PutS(HdmiAudioErrorText()) : PutNl()
    ProcedureReturn 4
  EndIf
  PutS("started: ") : PutDec(#TONE_RATE) : PutS(" Hz, ")
  PutDec(#TONE_CHANNELS) : PutS(" channels, N = ")
  PutDec(HdmiAudioProgrammedN()) : PutNl()
  PutS("  MAI_SMP divider N = ") : PutDec(HdmiAudioSmpN())
  PutS(", M = ") : PutDec(HdmiAudioSmpM()) : PutNl()
  PutNl()

  ; ------------------------------------------------------------------
  ;  THE MEASUREMENT. The real result of this program.
  ; ------------------------------------------------------------------
  PutS("--- MEASURED: how fast does the FIFO drain? ---") : PutNl()
  f0 = HdmiAudioFrameCount()
  rate = MeasureDrain(#DRAIN_WORDS)
  f1 = HdmiAudioFrameCount()

  PutS("  measured  ") : PutDec(rate) : PutS(" words per second") : PutNl()
  PutS("  predicted 96000  (108000000 / 2250 * 2 channels)") : PutNl()
  PutS("  frames elapsed during the burst: ")
  PutDec((f1 - f0) & $FFFFFFFF) : PutNl()

  If rate = 0
    PutS("  VERDICT: NOTHING IS DRAINING THE FIFO.") : PutNl()
    PutS("  Either the MAI is not running or the CPU may not write") : PutNl()
    PutS("  MAI_DATA. Do not go on to the tone - stop and find out") : PutNl()
    PutS("  which, because no sample value can fix either one.") : PutNl()
    HdmiAudioStop()
    ProcedureReturn 5
  EndIf

  ; Deliberately loose bands. The exact number will not be 96000 - the
  ; priming fill, the counter's granularity and the polling loop all
  ; move it by a fraction of a percent - and a gate that demanded
  ; equality would be a gate that always failed.
  If rate > 90000 And rate < 102000
    PutS("  VERDICT: 96000. The 108 MHz clock is real, MAI_SMP holds") : PutNl()
    PutS("  the divider we think it does, the CPU may feed MAI_DATA,") : PutNl()
    PutS("  and one word is one IEC 60958 subframe. Four inferences") : PutNl()
    PutS("  settled without believing a single status bit.") : PutNl()
  EndIf
  If rate > 45000 And rate < 51000
    PutS("  VERDICT: 48000, not 96000. The clock and the divider are") : PutNl()
    PutS("  right and the CPU may feed the FIFO, but ONE WORD IS A") : PutNl()
    PutS("  WHOLE STEREO FRAME - the subframe reading is wrong.") : PutNl()
    PutS("  Segment 4 below is the one to listen for.") : PutNl()
  EndIf
  If rate >= 102000
    PutS("  VERDICT: FASTER THAN PREDICTED. The MAI is running at a") : PutNl()
    PutS("  rate nobody programmed, or words are being discarded") : PutNl()
    PutS("  rather than played. Suspect MAI_SMP first.") : PutNl()
  EndIf
  If rate <= 45000
    PutS("  VERDICT: SLOWER THAN PREDICTED. Suspect the 108 MHz fixed") : PutNl()
    PutS("  clock assumption, then MAI_SMP. Do not touch the samples.") : PutNl()
  EndIf
  If rate >= 51000 And rate <= 90000
    PutS("  VERDICT: BETWEEN THE TWO PREDICTIONS AND NEAR NEITHER.") : PutNl()
    PutS("  That is the least informative answer and the most likely") : PutNl()
    PutS("  to mean the polling loop, not the hardware, set the pace.") : PutNl()
  EndIf

  PutS("  underrun latch after the burst: ") : PutDec(HdmiAudioUnderran()) : PutNl()
  PutS("  overrun latch after the burst:  ") : PutDec(HdmiAudioOverran()) : PutNl()
  HdmiAudioClearErrors()
  PutNl()

  ; ------------------------------------------------------------------
  ;  THE TONE. Five segments, announced.
  ; ------------------------------------------------------------------
  PutS("--- NOW LISTEN. Five bursts of 1 kHz, half a second each, ---") : PutNl()
  PutS("--- a quarter second of silence between them.             ---") : PutNl()
  PutS("--- Report WHICH ONES you heard, or that you heard none.  ---") : PutNl()
  PutNl()

  which = 1
  While which <= #SEGMENTS
    PutS("  segment ") : PutDec(which) : PutS(": ")
    PutEncName(which) : PutNl()
    ok = PlaySegment(which)
    If ok = 0
      PutS("  segment ") : PutDec(which) : PutS(" did not finish.") : PutNl()
    EndIf
    If HdmiAudioUnderran() <> 0
      PutS("    (underran - the CPU could not keep up)") : PutNl()
    EndIf
    If HdmiAudioOverran() <> 0
      PutS("    (overran)") : PutNl()
    EndIf
    HdmiAudioClearErrors()
    which = which + 1
  Wend

  ; ------------------------------------------------------------------
  ;  Down, leaving the picture exactly as it was found.
  ; ------------------------------------------------------------------
  HdmiAudioStop()
  PutNl()
  PutS("=== stopped. The picture should be untouched. ===") : PutNl()
  PutNl()
  PutS("WHAT THIS RUN PROVED BY ITSELF: the registers took their") : PutNl()
  PutS("values, the FIFO drained at a measured rate, the error") : PutNl()
  PutS("latches stayed clear and FRAME_COUNT advanced throughout.") : PutNl()
  PutS("WHAT IT CANNOT PROVE: that a sound came out. Only you can") : PutNl()
  PutS("say that, and a status bit must not be allowed to stand in") : PutNl()
  PutS("for you saying it.") : PutNl()
  ProcedureReturn 0
EndProcedure
